# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GETTING STARTED
#   1. Copy this file:  cp prd.md.example prd.md
#   2. Replace the example content below with your own PRD
#   3. Run:   npm run analyze-prd -- --file prd.md
#   4. Review prd-tests.txt, delete suggestions you don't want
#   5. Run:   npm run generate -- --file prd-tests.txt
#
# prd.md is gitignored — it is your local working file and will not be committed.
#
# SUPPORTED INPUT FORMATS
#   Text / Markdown  (.md .txt)
#     npm run analyze-prd -- --file prd.md
#
#   PDF  (.pdf)  — Claude reads it natively, layout and tables preserved
#     npm run analyze-prd -- --file spec.pdf
#
#   Image  (.png .jpg .jpeg .gif .webp)  — wireframe, mockup, or screenshot
#     npm run analyze-prd -- --file wireframe.png
#
#   Text + supplementary images
#     npm run analyze-prd -- --file prd.md --images wireframe.png,mockup.jpg
#
#   PowerPoint / Excel / Word
#     Export to PDF first, then: npm run analyze-prd -- --file spec.pdf
#
# WHAT THE TOOL DOES
#   • Classifies every feature by risk: critical → high → medium → low
#   • Generates happy-path AND negative/edge-case test suggestions for each
#   • Filters out tests already recorded in TEST_CASES.md (genuine gap list only)
#   • Writes prd-tests.txt in the same batch format as my-test.txt so you can
#     run `npm run generate -- --file prd-tests.txt` with no reformatting
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Example PRD — Shopping Cart

## Overview

Users can add products to a shopping cart, update quantities, and proceed to
checkout. Cart contents are visible across page navigations within the same session.

---

## User Stories

### US-01 — Add product to cart

As a shopper, I want to add products to my cart so I can buy multiple items in one order.

**Acceptance criteria:**
- Clicking "Add to Cart" on a product adds one unit
- The cart icon in the nav reflects the updated item count
- Adding the same product again increments its quantity rather than creating a
  duplicate entry
- A modal or confirmation confirms the item was added

### US-02 — View cart contents

As a shopper, I want to review my cart before purchasing.

**Acceptance criteria:**
- Cart page shows: product image, name, unit price, quantity, and line total
- Total amount equals the sum of all line totals
- An empty cart shows a friendly empty-state message, not a blank page

### US-03 — Remove an item from cart

As a shopper, I want to remove items I've changed my mind about.

**Acceptance criteria:**
- Each item has a delete/remove action
- Removing the last item shows the empty cart state
- Total updates immediately after removal without a page refresh

### US-04 — Proceed to checkout

As a shopper, I want to move from the cart to checkout when I'm ready to pay.

**Acceptance criteria:**
- "Proceed To Checkout" button navigates registered users to the checkout page
- Guest users see a modal prompting them to Register or Login before continuing
- The button is not shown when the cart is empty
